Bundled in the installers
=========================

The installers and the Linux archive (built by .github/workflows/release.yml from
packaging/map-vietnam.spec) carry third-party software next to the app, in the program folder
(for example "Map Vietnam/_internal" on Linux). Running from a source checkout installs the same
packages with pip instead, from requirements.txt and requirements-qt.txt. The licence files of the
bundled Python packages are copied into the app's licenses/ folder at build time, one folder per
package; the licence texts for Qt are in licenses/qt/ and CPython's is in licenses/python/. Each
package's source is on PyPI and at the address given.

Python, windowing
  CPython 3.12 (the interpreter and standard library): Python Software Foundation License
  (https://docs.python.org/3/license.html). Source: https://www.python.org/downloads/source/
  pywebview: BSD 3-Clause. Source: https://github.com/r0x0r/pywebview
  bottle (pywebview's helper): MIT. Source: https://github.com/bottlepy/bottle
  proxy_tools (pywebview's helper, by Jonathan Tushman): MIT, as its package metadata states; the
  package carries no licence file. Source: https://github.com/jtushman/proxy_tools
  pythonnet and clr_loader (Windows only, pywebview's link to the .NET window): MIT.
  Source: https://github.com/pythonnet/pythonnet, https://github.com/pythonnet/clr-loader
  (The Windows app shows its page in Microsoft's WebView2 runtime, which is part of Windows or
  installed by Microsoft; it is not included.)
  PyObjC (macOS only, pywebview's link to WKWebView): MIT. Source: https://github.com/ronaldoussoren/pyobjc

Qt (Linux only)
  PySide6, Shiboken6 and the Qt libraries inside them (QtCore, QtGui, QtWidgets, QtNetwork,
  QtWebChannel, QtWebEngine): GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (texts in licenses/qt/; the
  LGPL is written as additions to the GPL v3, so both are given). Qt WebEngine is built on Chromium
  and bundles its own third-party parts, each under its licence, listed by The Qt Company at
  https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/qtwebengine-attribution.html. The PySide6 and Shiboken6 packages
  (copyright The Qt Company Ltd.) carry no licence file of their own, only the licence name
  (LGPL v3, GPL v2 or GPL v3, at the user's choice; this app uses the LGPL v3). Qt's modules that
  are GPL v3 or commercial only, such as Qt Virtual Keyboard, are removed from the build by the spec.
  QtPy (the layer between pywebview and Qt): MIT.
  Source: Qt and PySide6 source code is at https://download.qt.io/official_releases/ (PySide6 at
  https://code.qt.io/cgit/pyside/pyside-setup.git/) and https://github.com/qtproject.
  Replacing or relinking Qt: the Linux app is a folder, not a single file, and Qt is kept as
  separate shared libraries (PySide6/Qt/lib/*.so, libpyside6*.so and libshiboken6*.so in
  "_internal"). To use a modified Qt or PySide6, build it from the source above and put the
  libraries in their place, or install the matching PySide6 wheels (requirements-qt.txt) and run
  the app from source with "python3 start.py". Map Vietnam does not modify Qt. PyQt is not used or
  included, because its licence (GPL v3 or commercial) does not allow it here.

Maps and imagery
